// Title: Microsoft Office DLL Sideload
// Sigma ID: 829a3bdf-34da-4051-9cf4-8ed221a8ae4f
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), Wietze Beukema (project and research)
// Date: 2022-08-17 | Modified: 2023-03-15
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, execution, stealth, T1574.001
// Description: Detects DLL sideloading of DLLs that are part of Microsoft Office from non standard location
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://hijacklibs.net/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_side_load_office_dlls.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\outllib.dll" and (not((FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft Office\\OFFICE" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft Office\\OFFICE" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft Office\\Root\\OFFICE" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft Office\\Root\\OFFICE")))
